proc finds, inspects and stops processes and ports with one command you
would guess on the first try. Target a process by port (:3000), PID, name
or path, see what holds a port and why it is there, and free it. Commands
that change anything ask first, preview with --dry-run, and print JSON with
stable exit codes for scripts and coding agents. On FreeBSD it reads ports
with sockstat(1) and open files with fstat(1).
